Codex (CLI + App) loads this skill at `.codex/skills/task-handoff/SKILL.md`
and activates it via the skill loader (`$task-handoff` or `/skills`). The
Codex subagent TOML `developer_instructions` includes a one-line pointer to
this skill plus the 12-field fail-closed guard so subagents reject malformed
assignments even when the skill is not pre-loaded.

## Per-runtime delegation surfaces (host side reference)

| Runtime | Native delegation surface |
|---|---|
| Copilot CLI | Task / agent tool fan-out (optional `/fleet` for independent batches) |
| Claude Code | `Agent` tool calls (multiple in one assistant turn for parallel-safe siblings) |
| OpenCode | `task` permission + `@<agent-name>` routing, gated by `permission.task` in `opencode.json` |
| OpenAI Codex (CLI + App) | child agent threads; `.codex/config.toml` `[agents] max_threads` caps concurrency; `max_depth = 1` is the safe default |
| Gemini CLI | root-session fan-out only; Gemini subagents cannot recursively call other subagents |
